er/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439862} :answer-field/id #uuid "30e09a55-e1b1-529e-9575-29c8323f08a4" :answer-field/key "III" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440288} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "5278cce0-690a-57d3-9f99-59786668dd25" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439863} {:answer/id #uuid "c194ddff-249d-568f-bbed-b5a98a9cbf2b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439864}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c194ddff-249d-568f-bbed-b5a98a9cbf2b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439864} :answer-field/id #uuid "4f6cf21c-f929-519d-97e8-9c947398a3c9" :answer-field/key "IV" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440289} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "fd09c21d-1862-5911-bc93-7b66b39ffdd2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439865} {:answer/id #uuid "800ae177-fe54-5efa-bdce-f8e4327de277" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "true" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439866}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "fd09c21d-1862-5911-bc93-7b66b39ffdd2" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "false" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186439865} :answer-field/id #uuid "50868321-e216-553a-b3ca-72efe4f524e3" :answer-field/key "V" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186408166 :db/ident :answer-field.type/checkbox} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186440290}] :question/id #uuid "142e660e-5b1f-5e61-a343-ee1945f69615" :question/math-academy-id "q-65208" :question/problem "At which points on the curve $9x^{2}y = 3y^{3} - 6x$ is the tangent vector to the curve perpendicular to the vector $i$?\n\nSelect all that apply. If none apply, leave all boxes unchecked.\n\n- **I.** $(-1,-1)$\n- **II.** $(-1,1)$\n- **III.** $(0,0)$\n- **IV.** $(1,-1)$\n- **V.** $(1,1)$" :question/worked-solution "Write the curve as F(x,y)=0. A tangent is (F_y,-F_x); its dot product with the given vector is $9 x^{2} - 9 y^{2}$. Solving this with the curve equation gives $(-1,1), (0,0), (1,-1)$, and the tangent is nonzero at each point."}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186500338 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186124456 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "84245283-3cf9-5889-8c42-896a0c8af291" :knowledge-point/title "Finding the Points on a Curve at which the Tangent Vector is Perpendicular to a Given Vector"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0b0c0406-ae8d-54c8-b629-8afd582156ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(-2,2)$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499678} {:answer/id #uuid "23b36d38-920a-5a19-90af-0d58ea66b6c1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(2,2)$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499733} {:answer/id #uuid "4e379d7d-a44b-5b19-ae49-edc70a8dad28" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(-\\sqrt[3]{4},\\sqrt[3]{4})$ and $(\\sqrt[3]{4},-\\sqrt[3]{4})$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499802} {:answer/id #uuid "930ec2dc-3268-5e8c-bb20-3557f9ac1938" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(-\\sqrt[3]{4},\\sqrt[3]{4})$ and $(-2,-2)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499942} {:answer/id #uuid "fd6ba7c0-fd84-5eed-9805-7ee46c6511bf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(-\\sqrt[3]{4},\\sqrt[3]{4})$ and $(2,2)$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500174}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0b0c0406-ae8d-54c8-b629-8afd582156ce" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$(-2,2)$ only" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186499678} :answer-field/id #uuid "956e93fd-6df8-5b5f-8f5c-3b6f83220074" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186500239}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "a5f3b132-60d1-51a8-b2e5-d8b20ae5add9" :question/math-academy-id "q-65209" :question/problem "At which points on the curve $3y{x}^{2}=48+3x{y}^{2}$ is the tangent vector to the curve perpendicular to the vector $i-j?$" :question/worked-solution "First, we bring all variables to one side:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3y{x}^{2} & =48+3x{y}^{2} \\\\ 3y{x}^{2}-3x{y}^{2} & =48\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nIf we set $f(x,y)=3y{x}^{2}-3x{y}^{2}$, our curve can be viewed as the level curve $f(x,y)=48.$ \n\nA tangent vector to the level curve can be computed as follows:\n\n$$\nt(x,y)={f}_{y}(x,y)\\,i-{f}_{x}(x,y)\\,j\n$$\n\nSo, we calculate $t(x,y):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}t(x,y) & ={f}_{y}(x,y)\\,i-{f}_{x}(x,y)\\,j \\\\  & =\\frac{∂}{∂y}(3y{x}^{2}-3x{y}^{2})i-\\frac{∂}{∂x}(3y{x}^{2}-3x{y}^{2})j \\\\  & =(3{x}^{2}-6xy)i-(6xy-3{y}^{2})j\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince our tangent vector needs to be perpendicular to $i$, we must have $t\\cdot (i-j)=0.$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}t(x,y)\\cdot (i-j) & =0 \\\\ ((3{x}^{2}-6xy)i-(6xy-3{y}^{2})j)\\cdot (i-j) & =0 \\\\ 3{x}^{2}-6xy+6xy-3{y}^{2} & =0 \\\\ 3{x}^{2}-3{y}^{2} & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}-{y}^{2} & =0 \\\\ (x-y)(x+y) & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $x=y$ or $x=-y.$ Substituting $x=y$ into the equation of our curve gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3y{x}^{2} & =48+3x{y}^{2} \\\\ 3y{y}^{2} & =48+3y{y}^{2} \\\\ 3{y}^{3} & =48+3{y}^{3} \\\\ 0 & =48\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince we get a false statement, we conclude that does not exist points of the form $(x,x)$ on the curve. Substituting $x=-y$ into the equation of our curve gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3y{x}^{2} & =48+3x{y}^{2} \\\\ 3y(-y)^{2} & =48+3(-y){y}^{2} \\\\ 3{y}^{3} & =48-3{y}^{3} \\\\ 6{y}^{3} & =48 \\\\ {y}^{3} & =8 \\\\ y & =\\sqrt[3]{8} \\\\ y & =2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally:\n\n- If $y=2$, we get $x=-2$ and the corresponding point is $(-2,2).$"}]}
